    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis critically examines the Biden administration's unprecedented seizure of billions in Afghan central bank assets following the return of the Taliban to power. It begins with a detailed history of Afghanistan’s relations with great powers, the American war in Afghanistan, and the contentious American withdrawal from Afghanistan in August 2021. Then, it explores the intricacies of the decision-making process that led to the Biden administration’s bold foreign policy maneuver, considering its legal, ethical, and geopolitical dimensions. This thesis shines a light on this opaque and underreported action by the Biden administration. It details the trajectory of the billions currently parked in the Afghan Fund, a charitable foundation in Switzerland, as well as the billions remaining in the United States as potential compensation for victims of the September 11, 2001 attacks. This thesis goes on to study the potential lessons that can be gleaned from this unique case study, such as the ramifications of treating adversaries’ assets in this way, retribution on behalf of American families, and the impact of such actions on larger foreign policy objectives in an era of evolving global threats. It also explains the broader picture of this move within the broader context of the Biden administration’s foreign policy. Finally, this thesis provides policy recommendations on how the Afghan Fund can be better optimized for its stated objectives.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Hundal, J. (2024). Frozen Funds and Geopolitical Gambits: Implications of the Biden Administration's Seizure of Afghan Central Bank Assets. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/bx240rk8260. https://doi.org/10.25740/bx240rk8260.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
